W2.10 — `--skip-anchors-gate` forwarding (lane D authors -> lane A applies)
===========================================================================

Contract-X1 handoff. Lane D does not edit `migrate-tableau.rb`; this file IS
the deliverable. 6 changed lines (budget: <=10), two hunks:

  1. DECLARE beside the sibling gate-waiver flags (the :287/:314/:337
     pattern) — REASON is a REQUIRED OptionParser argument, so a bare
     `--skip-anchors-gate` refuses exactly like the siblings.
  2. FORWARD beside the :1249-1255 pass-throughs — the REASON string rides to
     `assert-phase6-ran.rb`, which records it in `waivers.json` + the
     parity-final census and counts it against the waiver budget
     (gate :551 declare, :834 hides-table, :872/:951 census, :2553-2554 record —
     `test-anchors-waiver-gates.rb` already pins all of that gate-side).

Why: verified 0 hits for `skip-anchors-gate` in `migrate-tableau.rb` vs the
gate defining it at `assert-phase6-ran.rb:551`. A gate-13 block during
`--finalize` therefore forces a STANDALONE gate re-run to spend the waiver —
the finalize run is already dead: one guaranteed re-entry (REF-STAR class).

Base: applies cleanly on `origin/wave/1@308cf07f`
(`migrate-tableau.rb` blob 2283a7cd). Context lines chosen away from lane A's
W2.5/W2.6 regions to keep the rebase trivial.

